.SH NAME
CWE\-755 \- Improper Handling of Exceptional Conditions
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not handle or incorrectly handles an exceptional condition.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB5\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2020\-7247
OpenBSD OpenSMTPD, added 2022\-03\-25.
.PP
OpenSMTPD Remote Code Execution Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
smtp_mailaddr in smtp_session.c in OpenSMTPD, as used in OpenBSD and other products, allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary commands as root via a crafted SMTP session.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-04\-15.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2020\-7247
.SS CVE\-2021\-38003
Google Chromium V8, added 2021\-11\-03.
.PP
Google Chromium V8 Memory Corruption Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Google Chromium V8 Engine has a bug in JSON.stringify, where the internal TheHole value can leak to script code, causing memory corruption. This vulnerability could affect multiple web browsers that utilize Chromium, including, but not limited to, Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Opera.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2021\-11\-17.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2021\-38003
.SS CVE\-2022\-44698
Microsoft Defender, added 2022\-12\-13, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Microsoft Defender SmartScreen Security Feature Bypass Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Microsoft Defender SmartScreen contains a security feature bypass vulnerability that could allow an attacker to evade Mark of the Web (MOTW) defenses via a specially crafted malicious file.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2023\-01\-03.
.PP
